  "name": "nest-imported-brackets",
  "description": "Two genuinely messy outlines, taken from the real STL files in test/files/ that the M5 importer is tested against and scaled 4x to router-part size. Nothing here was drawn to make nesting look good: the swept arm fills 33% of its bounding box and the hooked link 47%, which is simply what those parts are. That is the whole point - a table saw pays for the box and a router pays for the outline, so this is the fixture where the two engines are furthest apart, and it is held out so no heuristic may be chosen by looking at it.",
